ameter': 'n', 'value': 3.14}], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator whose getValue(0) returns 6.86 (original delegate value 10.0 minus 3.14)', 'description': 'Confirm that Float/Double values are handled with proper precision.'}]}, {'group': 'minus(Number) with Short constant', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 7}], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator whose getValue(0) returns 8 (original delegate value 15 minus 7) and getValue(1) returns 13 (original delegate value 20 minus 7)', 'description': 'Validate that a Short (auto‑boxed from int literal) is correctly turned into a constant indicator and subtracted from a delegate that has different values at multiple indices.'}]}, {'group': 'minus(Number) with Byte constant (negative value)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': -2}], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator whose getValue(0) returns -3 (original delegate value -5 minus -2)', 'description': 'Check handling of a negative Byte constant; the subtraction should effectively add the absolute value.'}]}, {'group': 'minus(Number) with BigInteger constant', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': '12345678901234567890'}], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator whose getValue(0) returns -12345678901234567890 (original delegate value 0 minus the BigInteger constant)', 'description': 'Ensure that a BigInteger (passed as a Number via its toString representation) is accepted, converted to a Num, and subtracted without overflow.'}]}, {'group': 'minus(Number) with Double.NaN constant', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 'NaN'}], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator whose getValue(0) is NaN', 'description': 'When the constant is Double.NaN the resulting Num should also be NaN, propagating the undefined value.'}]}, {'group': 'minus(Number) with Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY constant', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 'Infinity'}], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator whose getValue(0) is -Infinity (original delegate value finite minus +Infinity)', 'description': 'Test subtraction of a positive infinite constant; the result must be negative infinite according to IEEE‑754 rules.'}]}, {'group': 'minus(Number) with custom Number subclass (AtomicInteger)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 'AtomicInteger(10)'}], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator whose getValue(0) returns 20 (original delegate value 30 minus 10)', 'description': 'Verify that any subclass of java.lang.Number (e.g., java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger) is correctly handled by createConstant.'}]}, {'group': 'minus(Number) chaining with plus(Number)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 5}], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator (result of minus(5).plus(3)) whose getValue(0) returns 48 (original delegate value 50 minus 5 plus 3)', 'description': 'Confirm that minus(Number) returns a NumericIndicator that can be further chained; the intermediate result should be correct.'}]}, {'group': 'minus(Number) on derived SMA indicator', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 2.5}], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator whose getValue(2) equals SMA(closePrice, 3) at index 2 minus 2.5', 'description': 'Apply minus(Number) to a non‑constant delegate (SMA of close prices). Verify subtraction works for a non‑trivial index (e.g., 2) where SMA has already performed averaging.'}]}]
